// Format : One 16-bit hex instruction/data value per line,
//          loaded starting at memory address 0.
//          Read by memory.v via $readmemh at synthesis time.
//
// Program (same one your testbench already runs):
//   Addr 0: LDA 5   -> AC <= M[5]
//   Addr 1: BUN 3   -> jump to address 3 (skips address 2)
//   Addr 2: LDA 6   -> should NEVER execute (proves BUN works)
//   Addr 3: STA 7   -> M[7] <= AC
//   Addr 4: HLT     -> opcode 111, halts (loops on itself)
//   Addr 5: 00AA    -> data operand for LDA
//   Addr 6: 00BB    -> data operand that must NOT get loaded
// ============================================================
2005
4003
2006
3007
7000
00AA
00BB
